xpf (0.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Dataplane: account status-poll health before discarding a stale-sequence
    reply, while keeping status publication fenced (#17728).

  * Routing: authorize rib-group peer returns from the route owner's
    import-rib destinations in the correct direction. Keep kernel rules
    and the AF_XDP mirror aligned, cover asymmetric imports, and clarify
    the deferred VRF-to-VRF forward-import warning (#17705).

  * Event engine: recheck live `trigger until` ceilings when draining recorded
    cooldown crossings, preventing parked storms from replaying over the
    ceiling while preserving short-window `trigger on` crossings (#17708).
  * Event engine: revalidate deferred cooldown replays against live
    `trigger until` ceilings immediately before commit if the worker waited
    on the config lock (#17696).
  * Daemon: bind commit-confirmed rollback-target pre-flight to the
    confirmation-window generation under the promotion lock, refusing a nested
    arm if a concurrent ConfirmCommit changed the target. Explicitly identify
    first-commit bootstrap targets, including a compiled empty tree after
    restart, and reject a missing non-first target (#17695).
  * Configstore: render commit summaries as individual set lines without
    cloning either tree or building both complete output strings; reuse
    equal lines so a 50k-line one-line edit stays under 10 MiB allocated
    (#17773).
  * Eventengine: keep a successor cooldown edge parked when a same-name
    policy is redefined during Apply's parked-entry purge window; validate
    captured revisions and replace stale same-key cooldown entries (#17709).
  * Cluster: release frozen IP-monitor debt when a configured secondary
    source address is not installed on its target interface (#17759).
    Confirmed absence releases stale debt; unconfirmed lookups preserve
    neutral treatment.
  * Config compiler: retain every independent single-rate policer-limit
    diagnostic in deterministic name order, including coexisting missing-limit
    and burst-floor defects on one policer (#17761).

  * Config: raise the shared two-/three-color policer burst floor to 1518
    bytes so a bucket admits a maximum-size VLAN frame at the default MTU
    (1500 MTU + 14-byte Ethernet header + 4-byte 802.1Q tag = 1518).
    Schema guidance and regression coverage now pin the tagged-frame floor
    (#17760).

  * API: derive REST session `ha_active` and `ha_state` from one HA ownership
    sample per row, preventing contradictory fields across a failover
    (#17752).
  * Config: fail closed for nonempty embedded change-configuration
    payloads that lex to no tokens or lose content to comments; recursively
    mask quoted comment-shaped command payloads and preserve the whole-payload
    placeholder through joined and block AST rewrites and compare fingerprints
    (#17813).
  * Logging: keep filter-term syslog routing bound to the applied snapshot
    generation across partial publishes (#17810).
  * Daemon: add already-MASTER sync-hold reconcile coverage with an
    authoritative VRRP manager instance retained through held, release-only,
    and steady-state passes (#17821).
  * Config: reject redundancy-group node statements without an explicit
    election priority at commit; tolerant loads warn and continue booting
    persisted configurations (#17820, following the #16672 node-shape gate).
  * VRRP: serialize both ordinary preempt kicks and cluster-authoritative
    `ForceRGMaster` against state transitions. The manager now checks the
    state, sets `forcePreemptOnce`, and queues its kick in one `vi.mu`
    critical section, preventing a delayed force from crossing MASTER
    entry/resignation drains and re-promoting a resigned node (#17827).
  * Coalesce/ipmon: ipmon actuation is single-flighted — the engine
    tick is the only Tick driver (the loop is started context-only,
    no second sweep goroutine), and Tick itself claims an in-flight
    slot so concurrent ticks can never enter the actuator together
    (#17226).
  * Coalesce: Loop.Stop now cancels the in-flight actuation context
    before waiting for the loop to exit, and the loop's context is
    parented on the StartWithContext caller (the daemon route
    listener passes its run ctx). A route-refresh actuation parked on
    the held apply semaphore now aborts on shutdown/run-ctx cancel
    instead of holding wg.Wait for the 30s actuate timeout past
    TimeoutStopSec=20; ipmon drops its private #3758 cancel and uses
    the loop's Context() (#17226).
  * Config compiler: parseVRRPGroups now reads every vrrp-group
    property exactly once. The Keys-packed tail and the child nodes
    are normalized into one statement list (vrrpGroupStatements)
    before the single remaining switch, deleting the second reader
    whose copies had diverged: on the packed hierarchical one-liner
    a legacy track-priority-cost could overwrite a nested
    priority-cost by source order, and a bad packed sibling erased
    a good nested cost to 0 on the lenient path. Nested cost now
    wins regardless of spelling or order, and a bad sibling is
    ignored. A bare packed `preempt` no longer swallows the next
    property: its optional `hold-time <n>` pair is reserved only
    when the next token is literally `hold-time`, so
    `preempt priority 200` keeps priority 200 and
    `preempt no-preempt` stays non-preempting instead of inverting
    (#17227).
  * Linuxsock/LLDP/proxy-ARP: add one shared cancellable raw-receive
    primitive (linuxsock.PpollRecv: ppoll on {socket, wake eventfd},
    SignalStop wakes, close only after join) and migrate both raw
    receive loops onto it. The proxy-ARP responder previously parked
    in a bare Recvfrom whose only wake was closing the fd (which does
    not wake a parked Recvfrom on Linux) and tore down cancel+delete
    with no join, leaking the goroutine and its bound socket on a
    silent link and answering the next request from its stale
    snapshot through a reused fd number; teardown now signals, joins,
    then closes, and the loop re-checks ctx after every successful
    recv before sending. LLDP keeps its #16669 behaviour on the shared
    primitive. A new linuxsock AST canary rejects direct blocking
    Recvfrom outside the primitive (nfqueue poll-guarded reads
    allowlisted) (#17231).
 -- xpf maintainers <noreply@anthropic.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

xpf (0.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Config: build lenientCompileOpts() with per-flag assignments instead
    of one gofmt-aligned ~330-key composite literal, and un-embed the
    formatting-workaround embedded struct into two plain compileOpts
    fields, so adding a long-named lenient flag changes exactly two
    lines instead of realigning the whole literal (#17168). No
    behavior change: the tolerant flag set is unchanged and the #4406
    golden compiled output is byte-identical to master.
  * Config reads: the rollback slot error now travels inside one
    captured value (configstore.RollbackCapture from CaptureRollback /
    CaptureRollbackSlot) through the REST, gRPC and CLI gates to their
    handlers, replacing the trailing positional slotErr every gate
    could blank and the second-lock RollbackSnapshotErr re-derivation
    (both getters deleted). REST /config/compare?rollback=N for a
    classed principal now answers 400 for a missing slot and for
    "not in configuration mode" instead of 200 "" ("no diff"), and
    gRPC ShowCompare surfaces the captured history error verbatim
    instead of a synthesized "slot not found" (#17215).
  * NFQUEUE reinject: write the P-MECH tail zone id as u32 in the Go
    submit encoder, matching both Rust readers widened by #17623
    (#16557); the u16 writer displaced every following field and every
    Go-produced frame failed decode. The P-MECH tail is 81 bytes, and
    a shared Go/Rust golden frame (zone id above the u16 range) now
    pins the wire so the pair cannot drift again (#18207).
