xpf (0.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Config compiler: strict mode now has a single constructor,
    strictCompileOpts() beside lenientCompileOpts(); the production
    strict entries and strict-named test compiles start from it
    instead of hand-copied compileOpts literals, so a future
    always-on strict fold cannot diverge from the tests that claim
    to measure the commit path (#17148).
  * HA: answer interface-ref → redundancy-group ownership from one
    SSOT (config.InterfaceRefRG / RefRG / RefRGIndex over
    RethRGOwners). RPM no longer name-tests `reth*`, so a structural
    bond0 RETH gates its ip-monitoring test on its own RG; the DHCP
    relay per-packet gate uses a cached RefRGIndex; proxy-ARP, IPsec,
    DDNS, DHCP lease, zone, RA, SNMP and RETH-MAC readers all share
    the answer, and a stray group on a non-RETH owns nothing (#17086).
  * HA: a declared dotted interface (#9821) with a set redundancy-group
    owns that group even with no members, so its zone RG resolves
    instead of dropping to group 0; undotted strays and non-numeric
    dotted names still own nothing (#17086).
  * Flow export: delete the production-dead ExportConfig sampling gates
    (ShouldExport, ShouldExportIface, ShouldExportIfaceDaemon,
    FlowDirection); SampledForOpen/SampledForClose are the single
    production gates on one eligible predicate, and tests now exercise
    them instead of the dead wrappers (#17061).
  * Upgrade: collect a deferred kernel prune on an ordinary boot without
    rewriting a slot selector that a later roll has repurposed (purge the
    obsolete candidate packages only), and reach that collector from the
    installed boot gate instead of only via a manual promote (#17860).
  * IPsec: restore the prior file only when its marker (if present) and complete
    loaded connection projection (names, children, local/remote addresses) prove
    the prior render. A live mismatch keeps the candidate but does not promote
    its fingerprints; stale SAs are torn down without re-initiation under the
    unproven config. Deferred eager-initiation debt is preserved until a later
    successful candidate load, which can re-initiate the changed tunnel even
    if its stale SA is no longer live. Unreachable or candidate-proven reloads
    keep and promote the candidate. Empty or malformed listings are not proof.
    Plain Apply uses a rendered-config fingerprint (#17882).
  * CLI/login-class: a deny alternative that merely touches the command
    core no longer disables the pipe-text veto (#17856). #16780's guard
    asked whether the whole deny pattern ever matched the pipe-less
    core, so the losing `^sh` branch of `deny-commands "^sh|display set"`
    let `show configuration | display set` run under `allow ^show` while
    the winning `display set` branch matched only pipe text. The guard
    now judges the branches realizing the deny's winning extent on the
    piped spelling, so that denial stands; core-winning exception
    geometry (`^show log 100$` beside `^show log$`, public-vrf) still
    saves through a benign pipe.
  * Upgrade: when a rolling rollback completes after a deferred signal,
    still wait for session sync and confirm rejoin before surfacing the
    signal status. Do not classify the committed rollback as destructive
    and leave the node ForceSecondary-drained (#17957).
  * DHCP: retain restart-before-seed ordering beyond the old 20-second
    fail-open deadline and re-age peer lease lifetimes before seeding
    (#17884).
  * Config: preserve distinct same-named IPsec traffic-selector fragments;
    normalize identical direct/chained selector bodies including block-valued
    local-ip and remote-ip leaves (#17802).
  * Userspace helper startup: retain and execute the validated helper inode
    through an inherited file descriptor, closing the pathname re-resolution
    window between validation and process start (#17881).
  * daemon: retain failed former-RETH permanent-MAC restorations for retry,
    surface restore failures as apply errors, preserve actual former-member
    identity across teardown renames and retire stale markers even when link-up
    fails, and retain confirmed/legacy MAC owners without absent-member debt (#17890).
  * Policy simulation: exempt from-zone junos-host queries from the
    v4-mapped/compatible IPv6 ingress-drop verdict. Locally-generated
    traffic egresses via the kernel TX path and never traverses the RX
    gate, so reporting an ingress drop fabricated a forwarding stage
    (#17865).
  * Config authorization: surface captured rollback slot errors before scoped
    subtree authorization on gRPC/REST reads. REST compare command pre-checks
    ignore ?path= as the handler does; command restrictions and invalid-
    argument statuses remain enforced (#17967).
  * FRR: remove the unused rewriteFRRPipeSequences belt. Community
    regexes, Junos AS-path regexes, and BGP neighbor descriptions
    handle vty pipe-space through their production translator or gate;
    the former shared-helper claim overstated its coverage (#17799).
  * NAT: allocate synthetic logical RETH VLAN ifindexes from the same
    sorted shared collision set in the session-scope folder as in the
    interface snapshot builder, preserving imported NAT scope identity
    when synthetic hash slots collide (#17876).
